        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.10.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.10.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "EZK.1.10"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ezek 1.10",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "REV.4.7"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Rev 4.7",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Each creature had four faces. The first was the face of a bull, the second a human face, the third the face of a lion, and the fourth the face of an eagle. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.10.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.10.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 10:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "(They were the same creatures that I had seen by the River Chebar.) When the creatures rose in the air ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.10.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.10.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 10:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and moved, the wheels went with them. Whenever they spread their wings to fly, the wheels still went with them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.10.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.10.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EZK 10:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When the creatures stopped, the wheels stopped; and when the creatures flew, the wheels went with them, because the creatures controlled them.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EZK.10.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EZK.10.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
